# Third-Party Licenses

Rumoca itself is licensed under the Apache License 2.0; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).

This file is the attribution notice for the third-party Rust crates whose code
is statically linked into the published `rumoca` and `rumoca-lsp` binaries.
Those binaries embed the code of the crates listed here, and every license
listed here conditions redistribution on its notice being reproduced.
Reproducing them, alongside the binary, is what discharges that condition.

The crate set is the workspace's default-feature runtime dependency graph
resolved over every published target. That is a superset of what any single
binary links, because a crate reachable only from another workspace member is
listed too. Over-attribution costs nothing; under-attribution is the failure
mode this file exists to prevent.

The file is generated, not hand-written. Regenerate it with
`infra/licenses/generate.sh`; the crate set and the accepted-license policy are
in `infra/licenses/about.toml`. Do not edit this file directly.

